    'tour_owner_step_stats_body' => 'Goods delivered today, orders today, and the payments and withdrawals waiting for you. Money figures count delivered goods only.',
    'tour_owner_step_stats_action' => 'Press a card to open the list behind it.',
    'tour_owner_step_stats_tip' => 'Clear waiting work within the day so partners are not kept waiting.',
    'tour_staff_step_stats_title' => 'Today\'s business',
    'tour_staff_step_stats_loc' => 'The row of cards at the top',
    'tour_staff_step_stats_body' => 'Today\'s numbers for your work: orders today, and payments and withdrawals waiting. You see only what your access allows.',
    'tour_staff_step_stats_action' => 'Press a card to open the list behind it.',
    'tour_staff_step_stats_tip' => 'Look at these numbers first thing in the morning.',
    'tour_office_trend_title' => 'Sales over two weeks',
    'tour_office_trend_loc' => 'Beside Today\'s work (below it on a phone)',
    'tour_office_trend_body' => 'Each bar is the value of goods delivered that day, for the last two weeks. The line above the bars shows this month\'s deliveries and orders.',
    'tour_office_trend_action' => 'Rest the pointer on a bar to see that day\'s amount.',
    'tour_office_trend_tip' => 'A day with no bar means nothing was delivered.',
    'tour_owner_step_domains_title' => 'The menu',
    'tour_owner_step_domains_loc' => 'Left side (on a phone, the menu button)',
    'tour_owner_step_domains_body' => 'One list in four blocks: daily work, money, products and partners, then staff, reports, website and settings. A row with several pages shows them as tabs at the top of the page.',
    'tour_owner_step_domains_action' => 'Press a row to open it. Type in “Search menu” to find a page.',
    'tour_owner_step_domains_tip' => 'Withdrawal requests and Commission rules & rates are rows of their own. Rarely used pages are in Settings.',
    'tour_staff_step_domains_title' => 'The menu',
    'tour_staff_step_domains_loc' => 'Left side (on a phone, the menu button)',
    'tour_staff_step_domains_body' => 'One list, with daily work first. You see only the rows and tabs your job allows. A row with several pages shows them as tabs at the top of the page.',
    'tour_staff_step_domains_action' => 'Press a row to open it. Type in “Search menu” to find a page.',
    'tour_staff_step_domains_tip' => 'A number beside a row means work is waiting there. If you need a page you cannot see, ask the owner for access.',
    'tour_office_treasury_title' => 'Treasury: all company money',
    'tour_office_treasury_loc' => 'Menu → Treasury',
    'tour_office_treasury_body' => 'One place for company money. Funds shows what came in, what went out and what each fund has now. Order report has one line per order. The event log, on the “Other modules” page, lists everything in time order. Partners\' money shows what each partner has. Money tasks is what is waiting for someone.',
    'tour_office_treasury_action' => 'Press “Treasury” in the menu, then press the tabs at the top.',
    'tour_office_treasury_tip' => 'Every money figure is worked out after delivery.',
    'tour_office_settings_title' => 'Settings',
    'tour_office_settings_loc' => 'Menu → Settings (the last row)',
    'tour_office_settings_body' => 'One page of links in three groups: Money, Areas and partners, and System. Account rules, bKash and bank numbers, login rules, courier connections and the work log are here.',
    'tour_office_settings_action' => 'Press “Settings”, then press a link.',
    'tour_office_settings_tip' => 'You see only the links you can open.',
    'tour_partner_buy_title' => 'Start here: New order',
    'tour_partner_buy_loc' => 'Shortcut buttons beside your account (below it on a phone)',
    'tour_partner_buy_body' => 'Quick buttons for your daily work: new order, my orders, deliveries, wallet and more.',
    'tour_partner_buy_action' => 'Press “New order”, pick products and send the order. Pay the full amount first: by bKash, Nagad, Rocket or bank with proof, in cash at the office, or from the money in your account.',
    'tour_partner_buy_tip' => 'Buy only from the company. Goods are sent only after the office checks your full payment.',
    'tour_partner_income_title' => 'Your income, head by head',
    'tour_partner_income_loc' => 'Below the shortcut buttons',
    'tour_partner_income_body' => 'One name for each income head, such as “Own purchase income” and “Referral income (direct)”, with the total so far.',
    'tour_partner_income_action' => 'Press a card to open Wallet with only that income in the list.',
    'tour_partner_income_tip' => 'To see every income head in one place, open “My account”. A head that received nothing shows ৳0.00.',
    'tour_partner_sidebar_title' => 'Menu',
    'tour_partner_sidebar_loc' => 'Left side (on a phone, the menu button)',
    'tour_partner_sidebar_body' => 'All pages: New order, My orders, Wallet, My team & customers, Contact the office, My account and Other modules. Prescriptions always stay in the menu.',
    'tour_partner_sidebar_action' => 'Press a row to open it. A row with several pages shows them as tabs at the top. Type in “Search menu” to find a page.',
    'tour_partner_sidebar_tip' => 'If you get stuck, Contact the office → Help has the user guide and a support form.',
    'getting_started_s1' => 'Know the address of your panel. The owner’s address starts with sadmin, staff with manage, dealers with dealer and sub-dealers with subdealer.',
    'getting_started_s2' => 'On the sign-in page, type your email or phone number. Then type your password and press “Log in”. Dealers and sub-dealers can also type their own code.',
    'getting_started_s3' => 'If a code comes to your phone or app, type that code.',
    'getting_started_s4' => 'For a new account, the office gives you a temporary password. The first time you sign in, the Security page opens by itself. Set your own new password there.',
    'getting_started_s5' => 'A short tour may start on the dashboard the first time. Watch it to the end.',
    'getting_started_s6' => 'Look at the top bar. You will see your name, the language button and the day and night button. Day (light) mode is on at the start.',
    'getting_started_s7' => 'Look at the numbers on the dashboard. If you must finish something first, a message appears at the top.',
    'getting_started_s8' => 'Bookmark only your own panel’s address. Never use the owner’s password in the staff panel.',
    'getting_started_s9' => 'If you cannot sign in, check the address and password again. If needed, press “Forgot password?”. If your account is suspended, call the office. If you are staff, check that the owner has given you permission.',
    'getting_started_o1' => 'You are in your own panel and you can see the parts you need for your work.',
    'getting_started_o2' => 'Only you know your password now.',
    'getting_started_o3' => 'You can open help from any page.',
    'getting_started_t1' => 'Choose Bangla or English with the language button. Your choice is saved.',
    'getting_started_t2' => 'If you get stuck, press the compass at the top. You will find this guide there. To see the tour again, press “Start the dashboard tour”.',
    'getting_started_t3' => 'Dealers and sub-dealers: open “Contact the office” and tell the office from “Help”.',
    'getting_started_w1' => 'Do not give your code or password to anyone. Not even if a staff member asks.',
    'getting_started_w2' => 'Do not put test (demo) data into the real system.',
    'profile_security_s1' => 'Open your profile. Dealers and sub-dealers: open “My profile” from the menu. It shows your name, parents’ names, date of birth, ID number (last 4 digits only), address and area of responsibility. Office staff: open it from the picture menu at the top.',
    'profile_security_s2' => 'Check that your name, shop name, phone, email and address are right.',
    'profile_security_s3' => 'If something is wrong, use “Fix my details” or “Ask for a change”. If the company has locked your profile, only the company can change it.',
    'profile_security_s4' => 'To show your identity, press “Download ID card”.',
    'profile_security_s5' => 'Open the security page. Dealers and sub-dealers: open “My profile”, then “Password & security”. Office staff: open “Account security” from the picture menu.',
    'profile_security_s6' => 'To change your password, type your present password in “Current password”. For a new account, type the temporary password the office gave you. Then type your new password in both boxes and press “Update password”.',
    'profile_security_s7' => 'Your new password must have at least 8 characters. Do not use 12345678, 11111111, your phone number or your own code.',
    'profile_security_s8' => 'On the security page, see which devices you are signed in on. If one looks strange, log it out.',
    'profile_security_s9' => 'If two-step sign-in (2FA) is on for staff, add the authenticator app. Write the recovery codes on paper and keep them safe.',
    'profile_security_o1' => 'Your profile details are correct. No wrong details go on invoices and ID cards.',
    'profile_security_o2' => 'Only you know your password. When you change it, you are logged out of your other devices.',
    'profile_security_o3' => 'You can shut out a strange device right away.',
    'profile_security_t1' => 'If you joined with a birth registration, send your NID number and a photo of the card from this page before your first withdrawal. The office will check it.',
    'profile_security_t2' => 'The office adds new members, so there is no join link or poster for partners now.',
    'profile_security_t3' => 'If a box in your profile is closed, tell the office. Once your NID is on file, dealers cannot change it themselves.',
    'profile_security_w1' => 'Nobody from the office will ask for your password. If someone asks, do not give it.',
    'profile_security_w2' => 'Do not email a copy of your NID. Upload it only in the panel.',
    'profile_security_w3' => 'When you finish work on someone else’s computer, log out.',
    'support_s1' => 'Press the compass at the top. This guide opens.',
    'support_s2' => 'Type one word in the search box. For example order, withdrawal or commission.',
    'support_s3' => 'Open the chapter and read it. It has separate parts: what it is, why it matters, what to do, what happens, tips and warnings.',
    'support_s4' => 'If a page is blocked, do first what the message tells you to finish.',
    'support_s5' => 'If you find no answer, send a help request. Dealers and sub-dealers: open “Contact the office”, then “Help”.',
    'support_s6' => 'Choose the topic. Write a title and the whole story. Give the order or withdrawal number. If needed, add a screenshot or PDF.',
    'support_s7' => 'Later, open your request. You will see its status and the office’s reply.',
    'support_s8' => 'Staff: open “Messages & support”, then “Support requests”. Go through them one by one, change the status and finish each with a clear reply.',
    'support_o1' => 'You get the answer to most “how do I” questions without waiting.',
    'support_o2' => 'Your request has enough detail, so staff can understand the problem easily.',
    'support_t1' => 'Search in Bangla or English, whichever you like.',
    'support_t2' => 'Write one problem in each request. It will reach the right person faster.',
    'support_t3' => 'To see the dashboard tour again, press “Start the dashboard tour” inside the guide.',
    'support_w1' => 'Do not write a password or a full NID number in a request.',
    'catalog_orders_s1' => 'To see all products and prices, open “Products & prices” from the menu. On the card of the product you need, press “Add to cart” and choose how many. If the product has more than one pack size, choose the size too. Press the cart icon at the top to open the cart. There you can change quantities, remove a product and see the total. Press “Place order” and every product moves to the order page. To take just one product, press “Order now”.',
    'catalog_orders_s2' => 'In the “Find a product” box, type the product name, code or pack size. Products appear as you type.',
    'catalog_orders_s3' => 'Choose the pack size. Type how many you need and add the product. If you come from the cart, the products are already filled in. The cart and the order page are the same list, so you never add anything twice. When the order is sent, the cart is emptied.',
    'catalog_orders_s4' => 'Look at the “Available now” number next to the product. If you ask for more, the rest becomes a “back order”. That means the rest will be sent later, when stock arrives.',
    'catalog_orders_s5' => 'Choose how to pay: bKash, Nagad, Rocket or bank. Or “By Office (cash at office)”. Or “From My Account”, which takes the money from the part of your Wallet you can use now.',
    'catalog_orders_s6' => 'Pay the full amount. The rule now is to pay in full when you order. For bKash, Nagad, Rocket or bank, type the TrxID and add a screenshot of the payment. For cash at the office, you write nothing more.',
    'catalog_orders_s7' => 'In the box “Check your order before it is sent”, look at the total in numbers and in words. If it is right, press “Yes, send the order”.',
    'catalog_orders_s8' => 'Write down the order number. Open the order from “My orders” in the menu and watch its status: Submitted, then Approved or Rejected, then Sent and Delivered.',
    'catalog_orders_s9' => 'On the order page, press “Download invoice”. Your copy may have a watermark. The company copy does not.',
    'catalog_orders_s10' => 'To cancel an order, open it and write your reason under “Cancel this order?”. Then press “Send the cancel request”. If your payment has not been checked yet, the order is cancelled at once. If it has, the office reviews it, cancels it and refunds you.',
    'catalog_orders_s11' => 'To return goods after they arrive, open “Return goods?”. Write which products and how many, and the reason. Then press “Send the return request”. The office takes the goods back and refunds you.',
    'catalog_orders_o1' => 'Your order gets a number. Prices come from today’s price list.',
    'catalog_orders_o2' => 'The office looks at the payment you sent and checks it.',
    'catalog_orders_o3' => 'When an order is cancelled or goods are returned, the goods, the money and the commission are all put right together. Money paid from your account goes back to your account.',
    'catalog_orders_t1' => 'Dealer and sub-dealer prices are different. If you see both, use the one for your account type.',
    'catalog_orders_t2' => 'The system stops the same order being sent twice. Still, wait for the first reply before you press again.',
    'catalog_orders_t3' => 'An old invoice number cannot be changed. If a line is wrong, send a correction request.',
    'catalog_orders_t4' => 'If you think a payment was counted short, first match the invoice total with the money you sent. Then tell Support.',
    'catalog_orders_w1' => 'Do not show a personal transfer as a company payment unless the money went to a published company account.',
    'catalog_orders_w2' => 'A product marked “Out of stock” or “Paused for now” cannot be ordered. Wait until stock comes back.',
    'catalog_orders_w3' => 'Once goods have started to be sent, you cannot cancel the order yourself. Tell the office. When the goods arrive, you can return them.',
    'catalog_orders_w4' => 'Do not order by chat or phone. If the order page is closed, send a support request.',
    'deliveries_dues_s1' => 'Open “Deliveries” under “My orders” in the menu. You see orders waiting to be sent and orders on the way.',
    'deliveries_dues_s2' => 'Look at the courier name and the tracking number. Give the number to the person who will receive the goods.',
    'deliveries_dues_s3' => 'When goods arrive, check the seal before you sign the courier challan. Count the goods against the invoice.',
    'deliveries_dues_s4' => 'When you hold the parcel, press “I received the goods” on the order page. This tells the office the goods arrived. The office is the one who confirms the delivery.',
    'deliveries_dues_s5' => 'If an order is still waiting to be sent, open it and check that your full payment was checked. Goods are not sent before that.',
    'deliveries_dues_s6' => 'If a payment was rejected, send the correct TrxID and screenshot again from the order page.',
    'deliveries_dues_s7' => 'If goods are short, take photos of the packet before you hand anything out. Then send a support request with the order number.',
    'deliveries_dues_s8' => 'If some goods are still not sent, the order says so. If it takes too long, ask the office to cancel the rest and refund you.',
    'deliveries_dues_o1' => 'You know which orders are on the way and which you have fully received.',
    'deliveries_dues_o2' => 'Goods are sent only after accounts staff have checked your full payment.',
    'deliveries_dues_o3' => 'Cancelled and returned orders stay on your Orders list, with the reason.',
    'deliveries_dues_t1' => 'A payment waiting to be checked does not count until it is checked.',
    'deliveries_dues_t2' => '“Delivered” only means the company has delivered to you. It has nothing to do with your own sales.',
    'deliveries_dues_w1' => 'Do not change courier labels. Report any mismatch right away.',
    'deliveries_dues_w2' => 'If you refuse a delivery, give a written reason with the order number.',
    'commissions_pool_s1' => 'Dealers and sub-dealers: open “Wallet”. Each card shows the total you earned from one kind of income.',
    'commissions_pool_s2' => 'Press a card. The list below then shows only that income.',
    'commissions_pool_s3' => 'Commission is added when the order is delivered. If only some goods arrive, commission is paid only on those goods.',
    'commissions_pool_s4' => 'If an order is cancelled or goods are returned, the commission on those goods is taken out too.',
    'commissions_pool_s5' => 'Office: open “Treasury” → “Order report”. Press an order. You see every commission line: the percent, the type, and who or which fund got it.',
    'commissions_pool_s6' => 'If staff give no commission on an order, that money goes to the company fund. The reason staff wrote is saved there.',
    'commissions_pool_s7' => 'In short: from each fully paid and delivered purchase the company keeps :dealer_company_rate% (dealer purchase) or :sub_company_rate% (sub-dealer purchase). The rest goes to the commission funds. It is shared among partners by the company rules.',
    'commissions_pool_o1' => 'Every taka of an order can be traced to a person or a fund.',
    'commissions_pool_t1' => 'On the Wallet list, pick dates to see one day, one month or any dates you choose.',
    'commissions_pool_w1' => 'The office sets the commission rates. Do not promise a partner any other rate.',
    'withdrawals_s1' => 'Open “Wallet” and press “Withdraw”.',
    'withdrawals_s2' => 'Choose “Take to bank or mobile”. Or choose “Order with this money”.',
    'withdrawals_s3' => 'Type the amount and your account number. Each method has a limit for one withdrawal. You can see the limit on the same form.',
    'withdrawals_s4' => 'When you send the request, the money is set aside. It cannot be spent until the office has checked it. The request stays on the “Wallet” page, so you can see what the office did.',
    'withdrawals_s5' => 'While the request is still waiting for the office, you can press “Cancel request”. The money comes back to your Wallet at once. After approval you cannot cancel. Then call the office.',
    'withdrawals_s6' => 'To order with this money, you go to the order page with “From My Account” already chosen. Nothing is taken until you place the order.',
    'withdrawals_s7' => 'Office: open “Withdrawal requests”, check the request and approve it. A finance staff member approves it, and another one sends the money. A withdrawal at or above the owner\'s limit (৳1,00,000 at the start) is approved only by the owner. The owner can approve and pay alone.',
    'withdrawals_s8' => 'Office: the person who sends the money adds the receipt. If there is no receipt yet, choose “Money sent, receipt later”. Then press “Add receipt” later.',
    'withdrawals_o1' => 'Every withdrawal has one line on the “Wallet” page. Once it is paid, the receipt is there too.',
    'withdrawals_o2' => 'If a request is cancelled before the money is sent, the money returns to your Wallet.',
    'withdrawals_t1' => 'Save your bank, bKash, Nagad or Rocket accounts in your profile under "My payout accounts" and pick one when you withdraw. Keep the numbers correct or the money may come back. After you change an account, withdrawals pause for a short while for your safety.',
    'withdrawals_t2' => 'If you have a TIN (tax number), you can save it on the withdraw form.',
    'withdrawals_w1' => 'For a short time after you change your phone number or password, you cannot ask for a withdrawal. This is usually 2 hours. It keeps your money safe if someone else gets into your account.',
    'withdrawals_w2' => 'If your account is suspended, your open requests are put on hold. No money is sent then. When the account is switched on again, the requests go on.',
    'withdrawals_w3' => 'Before your first withdrawal, the office must have your NID number on file. If it is missing, send the number and a photo of the card from your profile or the withdrawal page; withdrawals open once the office has checked it.',
    'withdrawals_w4' => 'If you do not see the “Withdraw” button, read the notice on the page. It tells you why.',
    'reports_s1' => 'Dealers and sub-dealers: the Dashboard has report tabs at the bottom. Press “Total report” to see all income. A single income tab shows only that income.',
    'reports_s2' => 'Open “Wallet” and use the search, filters and dates on the list.',
    'reports_s3' => 'Use “Download” for your statement, the “Full report (PDF)” and certificates.',
    'reports_s4' => 'Office: open “Treasury” → “Order report”. Press a row to see where every taka of that order went.',
    'reports_s5' => 'Office: use “Download” on the Order report to get files. You are offered only the files your job allows.',
    'reports_o1' => 'The figures on the screen and in the file are the same.',
    'reports_t1' => 'Money figures count delivered goods only.',
    'reports_w1' => 'Files have names and money figures. Do not give them to anyone outside the office.',
    'money_rules_s1' => 'Only purchases that are fully paid and delivered count.',
    'money_rules_s2' => 'Own purchase income: the buyer gets :cashback_rate% of their own purchase back.',
    'money_rules_s3' => 'Referral income (direct) and D2D income: the person who brought the buyer gets :referral_rate%. The two people above them get :gen2_rate% (2nd generation) and :gen3_rate% (3rd generation). If nobody is above, that share goes to company profit.',
    'money_rules_s4' => 'Area dealer income: :area_rate% is shared among the area dealers of the buyer’s place codes. Management :area_management%, division :area_division%, district :area_district%, upazila :area_upazila%, union or pourashava :area_union%. If a place has no area dealer, that share goes to company profit.',
    'money_rules_s5' => 'Monthly salary (dealer): :dealer_salary_rate% goes into the salary fund of the buyer’s division. Dealers there who buy at least :dealer_salary_min that month share it equally.',
    'money_rules_s6' => 'Rank royalty: :royalty_rate% is shared each month. It goes to dealers who keep their rank. You get royalty only for your latest rank.',
    'money_rules_s7' => 'Rank income and rank incentive: :incentive_rate% builds the incentive fund. The one-time “rank income” (MO, AM, SM, ME) is paid as soon as you reach a rank. If you reach MO and AM in the same month, you get both.',
    'money_rules_s8' => 'Marketing (:marketing_rate%) and the bike and car incentive funds (:vehicle_rate%) are company funds. They are for campaigns and big incentives.',
    'money_rules_s9' => 'Each month closes on its own. If a target (salary, area commission, royalty and so on) is missed, that month’s money goes to company profit. The reason is written down. This money does not move to the next month.',
    'money_rules_s10' => 'Only three funds build up from month to month: the rank award fund, the sub-dealer tour fund and the bike and car fund.',
    'money_rules_s11' => 'If your account is suspended, your commission is held. You see it on the “Wallet” page under “Commission held for you”. When the account is switched on again, the money comes to you by itself. If an account is closed, commission held for more than 3 months goes to company profit.',
    'money_rules_o1' => 'You can tell which money comes at once and which waits for month end.',
    'money_rules_o2' => 'You know that if you miss a target, that month’s share is lost. It is not saved for later.',
    'money_rules_t1' => 'Press “See my progress” on the Dashboard to see how close you are to each monthly target.',
    'money_rules_t2' => 'If the owner changes a rate, this page shows the new rate.',
    'money_rules_w1' => 'Do not wait for next month to make up a missed target. Each month is counted on its own.',
    'my_money_tabs_s1' => 'At the top you see how much you can use now, how much is waiting, and how much is in withdrawal requests.',
    'my_money_tabs_s2' => 'Press an income card, such as “Referral income (direct)”. The list below shows only that income. To see the heads that received nothing too, open “My account”.',
    'my_money_tabs_s3' => 'Use the search, filters and dates on the list.',
    'my_money_tabs_s4' => 'If some commission is held, you see it under “Commission held for you”. This money has not reached your balance yet.',
    'my_money_tabs_s5' => 'Press “Withdraw” to take money out or order with it. Press “Download” to get files.',
    'my_money_tabs_o1' => 'You can see, withdraw and check your money from one page.',
    'my_money_tabs_t1' => 'The same income list is also on your Dashboard. To see every head, including ৳0.00 ones, open “My account” in the menu.',
    'my_money_tabs_w1' => 'If you do not see “Withdraw”, read the notice on the page. It tells you why.',
    'rewards_milestones_s1' => 'Partners: press “See my progress” on the Dashboard. You see each target there. Team sales needed now: bike :bike_target, car :car_target.',
    'rewards_milestones_s2' => 'Only orders that are fully paid and delivered count, from your whole team since the start. Each direct line counts up to a limit: :bike_cap for the bike, :car_cap for the car.',
    'rewards_milestones_s3' => 'The bike fund and the car fund are separate. A reward is paid from its own fund. These funds are not lost at month end. They build up from month to month.',
    'rewards_milestones_s4' => 'Staff: open “Treasury” → “Spending, budgets & pending work” → “Rewards” to pay a reward. Write the method and a reference so a receipt can be made.',
    'rewards_milestones_s5' => 'Before you ask Support, check the progress bar and your eligible sales.',
    'rewards_milestones_s6' => 'Owner: set the prize amount for the bike and the car. Without it, a reward cannot be approved. Keep the money owed for rewards apart from daily running cash.',
    'rewards_milestones_o1' => 'Progress counts only eligible sales.',
    'rewards_milestones_o2' => 'Reward payments are recorded in the month-closing pages.',
    'rewards_milestones_t1' => 'Take photos of award papers and circulars and keep them.',
    'rewards_milestones_t2' => 'Reward items are separate from the money you can withdraw.',
    'rewards_milestones_w1' => 'Do not promise unfinished targets to others as guaranteed money.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s1' => 'Press “See my progress” on your Dashboard. You see the salary you have earned but not yet received.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s2' => 'Open “Wallet” and choose “Monthly salary” in the list filter. You see the salary money lines.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s3' => 'Every purchase that is fully paid and delivered counts toward your salary. There is no minimum amount.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s4' => 'After the month-end close, check that the money shows on Wallet.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s5' => 'The tour fund builds up on its own. It is not mixed with the money you can withdraw. It does not go back to zero when a month closes.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s6' => 'Dealers with sub-dealers: help them plan their sales. Do not lend your own cash against their future salary.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s7' => 'Staff: run the month-end salary from “Treasury” → “Spending, budgets & pending work” → “Month close”. Match each salary line with the order behind it.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s8' => 'If the salary is recorded but does not match your delivered sales, send a support request.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_o1' => 'You can see how much salary you have earned this month but not yet received.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_o2' => 'Paid amounts match the month-end accounts.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_o3' => 'The tour fund is kept apart from money you can withdraw.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_t1' => 'Keep your invoices. Each fully paid and delivered order adds to that month’s salary.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_t2' => 'Watch circulars for short-term salary offers or changes.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_w1' => 'The tour fund is not money to withdraw. The office uses it to send you on company tours.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_w2' => 'Staff must not change salary percentages outside the “Commission rules & rates” page.',
    'network_genealogy_s1' => 'Open “My team & customers” from the menu.',
    'network_genealogy_s2' => 'Copy your code, or share your QR code.',
    'network_genealogy_s3' => 'Send interested people to the joining form on the website, with your code.',
    'network_genealogy_s4' => 'See who is in your team and who is active.',
    'network_genealogy_s5' => 'To find someone, type a name, code or phone number in the box at the top.',
    'network_genealogy_s6' => 'To keep the list, press “Download team list (CSV)”.',
    'network_genealogy_s7' => 'Staff and owner: open the “Who is under whom” page in the office to see the whole team.',
    'network_genealogy_s8' => 'Staff and owner: check that each new member sits under the right referrer.',
    'network_genealogy_o1' => 'New dealers join your team with your code.',
    'network_genealogy_o2' => 'You see your whole team in one place.',
    'network_genealogy_o3' => 'You can use the downloaded list to help your team.',
    'network_genealogy_t1' => 'Use the same code for every campaign, so the records do not get mixed up.',
    'network_genealogy_t2' => 'Referral commission is paid only when the order is fully paid and delivered. The direct referrer gets :referral_rate%, the next one up gets :gen2_rate%, and the one above that gets :gen3_rate%. If a level has no referrer, that share goes to the company profit fund.',
    'network_genealogy_t3' => 'An area dealer earns by area. This has nothing to do with the referral team.',
    'network_genealogy_w1' => 'Never ask for anyone else\'s password, and never keep it.',
    'network_genealogy_w2' => 'If you think one person has opened more than one account, tell support. Send proof with it.',
    'ranks_royalties_s1' => 'Open “Rank” from the menu. Or press “See my progress” on the dashboard.',
    'ranks_royalties_s2' => 'See which rank you hold now and what is left for the next one.',
    'ranks_royalties_s3' => 'The ranks in order: MO (Marketing Officer), AM (Area Manager), SM (Sales Manager), ME (Marketing Executive).',
    'ranks_royalties_s4' => 'For MO, your own purchases count. For AM, SM and ME, the active dealers in your team count. See the numbers in the tips below.',
    'ranks_royalties_s5' => 'You get a one-time reward as soon as you reach a rank. If you become MO and then AM in the same month, you get both rewards.',
    'ranks_royalties_s6' => 'At the end of each month, the royalty money is shared out. People who kept their rank that month get a share.',
    'ranks_royalties_s7' => 'If nobody qualifies for a rank, that royalty goes to the company profit fund.',
    'ranks_royalties_s8' => 'Staff and owner: see the rank rules on the commission rules page. Never give anyone a rank by hand.',
    'ranks_royalties_o1' => 'You know your rank now and what is left for the next one.',
    'ranks_royalties_o2' => 'You know the two kinds of money: the one-time reward and the monthly royalty.',
    'ranks_royalties_o3' => 'You can see your reward and royalty records in the wallet.',
    'ranks_royalties_t1' => 'MO: your own total purchases since you joined must reach :mo_target. The one-time reward is :mo_bonus. AM: you need :am_count active dealers of rank MO or higher within :rank_depth levels of your team. The reward is :am_bonus. SM: you need :sm_count of rank AM or higher. The reward is :sm_bonus. ME: you need :me_count of rank SM or higher. The reward is :me_bonus.',
    'ranks_royalties_t2' => 'To get royalty in a month, meet your rank\'s monthly purchase in that same month: MO :mo_keep, AM :am_keep, SM :sm_keep, ME :me_keep. For the first :grace_days days after a new rank, you get royalty without this.',
    'ranks_royalties_t3' => 'When you explain this to your team, show your own purchases and the team\'s purchases separately.',
    'ranks_royalties_w1' => 'Do not put an earlier date on an order to get a rank.',
    'ranks_royalties_w2' => 'Staff must not give anyone a rank by hand. It makes the records wrong.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_s1' => 'Under any prescription, press “Save as template” and give it a name.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_s2' => 'In “New prescription”, open “Start from a template” and choose one. The medicines and advice fill in by themselves.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_s3' => 'To see or delete your templates, open the “Templates” tab.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_s4' => 'You can also save food lists. In the “Food templates” part, write once what to eat and what to avoid for each illness.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_s5' => 'When you write a prescription, set a “Follow-up date”.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_s6' => 'See the “Patients to see again” at the top of the prescription tab. It shows who is due today and whose date has passed.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_s7' => 'When you have seen the patient, press “Seen”. The patient leaves the list.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_o1' => 'You get a notice when a patient is due to come back.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_t1' => 'Only you can see your templates.',
    'prescription_templates_followups_w1' => 'Choosing a template replaces what is already written. So choose the template first, then write.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s1' => 'Open the “New partner applications” menu. Choose “Dealer applications” or “Sub-dealer applications”.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s2' => 'Open one application. Read the warnings under “Check before approving”.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s3' => 'Pick the area from the lists. The area code (place code) fills in by itself. For a dealer, also look at the “Also make area dealer” box.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s4' => 'If everything is right, press “Approve”.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s5' => 'If something is wrong, press “Send back for correction”. If you do not accept it at all, press “Reject”. Write a reason either way. The applicant can see it.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s6' => 'Open the “Dealers & sub-dealers” menu. To add someone yourself, press “Add dealer” or “Add sub-dealer”.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s7' => 'Type the name in English. The Bangla name may fill in by itself. Fill in the other boxes and press “Add account & send SMS”.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s8' => 'Open “Staff list” in the “Staff” menu. Press “Add staff”. Fill in the boxes and choose the “Role” and the “Branch”.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s9' => 'To add an MD or Chairman, open the “MD and Chairman” list. Press “Add MD / Chairman”. Tick the confirmation box.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s10' => 'When a new account is made, the first password shows on the screen once. Write it down now and give it to that person.',
    'staff_people_accounts_o1' => 'After approval, the new dealer or sub-dealer gets a partner code.',
    'staff_people_accounts_o2' => 'The applicant uses the application number and mobile number on the “Application status” page to see the result. An SMS is sent too.',
    'staff_people_accounts_o3' => 'The new person must choose their own password the first time they sign in.',
    'staff_people_accounts_t1' => 'If “Also make area dealer” is ticked, the dealer earns the area share, even on their own purchases. If it is not ticked, they stay a normal dealer.',
    'staff_people_accounts_t2' => 'If the applicant\'s area is not in the list, first add its code in “Settings” → “Area codes”.',
    'staff_people_accounts_t3' => 'When someone\'s role changes, check their permissions on “Roles & permissions” the same day.',
    'staff_people_accounts_t4' => 'At first, an MD or Chairman can only view and download payroll. The owner gives any extra rights separately.',
    'staff_people_accounts_w1' => 'Photos and ID copies are not collected online. Check the original papers before you approve.',
    'staff_people_accounts_w2' => 'Never let several people share one staff login.',
    'staff_people_accounts_w3' => 'The first password is shown only once. Do not close the page before you write it down.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s1' => 'Open the “Check order payments” menu. Press the row of the payment you want to check.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s2' => 'See if the money really arrived. Match the amount, the method and the screenshot with the company\'s accounts.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s3' => 'If the money arrived, press “Confirm payment”. If not, press “Reject” and write the reason.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s4' => 'Open the order in the “Orders” menu. Under “Review this order”, look at the items, the prices and the “Can be sent now” count.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s5' => 'If the full payment is checked, choose “Approved” in the “Decision” box. Then press “Save decision”.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s6' => 'Choose the branch in “Send from which branch”. Type 0 for any item you will send later.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s7' => 'Pick a courier, or type the courier name and tracking number. Then press “Save dispatch details”.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s8' => 'When the goods have really arrived, press “Confirm delivery”.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s9' => 'If a partner asks to cancel or return, open “Cancel, return and refund” on the order. If it looks right, press “Approve”. If not, press “Turn down”.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s10' => 'When money goes back, a second staff member must open the order and press “I checked it, confirm”. If the refund is at or above the owner\'s limit (৳50,000 at the start), one of the two must be the owner. Only the owner (Super Admin) can finish it alone.',
    'staff_fulfillment_o1' => 'Goods can be sent for an approved order. The order ends when delivery is done.',
    'staff_fulfillment_o2' => 'Stock goes down in the branch the goods were sent from.',
    'staff_fulfillment_o3' => 'When an order is cancelled or returned, the goods go back into stock. The money and commission records are corrected too.',
    'staff_fulfillment_t1' => 'At the end of each day, open “Treasury” → “Order report”. Match the goods sent with the money received.',
    'staff_fulfillment_t2' => 'When you say no, write the reason politely. The partner can see it. Tell them what to do next.',
    'staff_fulfillment_t3' => 'If some goods are still to send, the order shows a box called “Some goods are still to send”. A warning comes after 7 days. If it is very late, you can choose “Close the rest and refund”.',
    'staff_fulfillment_w1' => 'You cannot approve an order from your own linked dealer account. Another staff member must do it.',
    'staff_fulfillment_w2' => 'Never skip the payment check “as a favour”.',
    'staff_fulfillment_w3' => 'Type the refund amount yourself. You cannot give back more than allowed. Read the amount in words carefully before you confirm.',
    'place_codes_admin_s1' => 'Open “Settings”. Choose “Area codes”.',
    'place_codes_admin_s2' => 'Choose a level from the tabs at the top, such as division, district, upazila or union.',
    'place_codes_admin_s3' => 'Press the “Add code” button.',
    'place_codes_admin_s4' => 'Type the place name. Choose the upper area. In the code box type only the number. MNHC is already in front.',
    'place_codes_admin_s5' => 'Press “Save code”.',
    'place_codes_admin_s6' => 'To fix a mistake, press “Edit”. For a code that will not be used any more, untick “Active”.',
    'place_codes_admin_o1' => 'Every area where the company works has a code in the list.',
    'place_codes_admin_o2' => 'When you add a dealer or sub-dealer, you can pick the right area from the list.',
    'place_codes_admin_t1' => 'If an applicant\'s area is not in the list, add its code here first.',
    'place_codes_admin_t2' => 'To search, type a code, a name or an upper area in the “Search” box.',
    'place_codes_admin_w1' => 'Do not change a code that is printed on a dealer\'s ID card. If you do, the card must be printed again.',
    'place_codes_admin_w2' => 'Do not give the same area to two dealers. Each upazila has only one dealer.',
    'courier_staff_s1' => 'Owner: switch on the couriers in “Settings” → “SMS and courier connections”. Dealers can pick only the couriers that are on.',
    'courier_staff_s2' => 'Approve the order. If the dealer picked a courier, stock goes down and the parcel is booked by itself.',
    'courier_staff_s3' => 'For a “Company decides” order, open the order. Pick a courier under “Book with a courier (optional)”. Or type the courier name and tracking number.',
    'courier_staff_s4' => 'If the booking fails, a notice comes under the bell at the top. Open the order and press “Try booking again”.',
    'courier_staff_s5' => 'To change the courier, open the order and go to “Change courier”. Choose the “New courier”.',
    'courier_staff_s6' => 'If you want, write a note for the dealer. Then press “Change courier”.',
    'courier_staff_s7' => 'Has the courier taken the parcel, but the step has not moved? Press “Mark picked up”.',
    'courier_staff_s8' => 'When the goods have really arrived, press “Confirm delivery”. The courier saying “Delivered” does not finish the order.',
    'courier_staff_o1' => 'The dealer gets a notice. If you wrote a note, the dealer sees it too.',
    'courier_staff_o2' => 'The order history keeps a record of every courier change.',
    'courier_staff_t1' => 'Goods usually go from the head office. If another branch was chosen on the order, they go from that branch.',
    'courier_staff_t2' => 'You can change the courier only before the booking is made, or after the courier refused it.',
    'courier_staff_t3' => 'These buttons are for staff who handle orders or stock. Nobody can press them on their own order.',
    'courier_staff_w1' => 'The parcel is booked as soon as you approve. So check the order carefully before you approve it.',
    'deliveries_board_s1' => 'Open “Deliveries” in the menu.',
    'deliveries_board_s2' => 'On the “To send” tab, see the orders waiting to be sent. It also shows how long the oldest order has been waiting.',
    'deliveries_board_s3' => 'On the “With courier” tab, see every parcel given to a courier. Press a tracking number to open the courier\'s own page.',
    'deliveries_board_s4' => 'Open the “Not booked” tab. The courier did not accept these parcels. The “Problem” column tells you why.',
    'deliveries_board_s5' => 'Press the order number to open the order. Press “Try booking again”. If that fails, use “Change courier”.',
    'deliveries_board_s6' => 'The page shows the branch picked in the top bar.',
    'deliveries_board_o1' => 'You can see at a glance how many parcels are at each step.',
    'deliveries_board_o2' => 'Once a booking is made, the order leaves the “Not booked” list.',
    'deliveries_board_t1' => 'When a booking fails, a notice also comes under the bell at the top.',
    'deliveries_board_t2' => 'The “Decision needed” tab shows only when a partly delivered order is still waiting for a commission decision.',
    'deliveries_board_w1' => 'If the “Problem” column says the courier gave no clear answer, the parcel may already be booked. Check the courier\'s own panel first. If it is there, do not book it again.',
    'parcel_received_back_s1' => 'Wait until the parcel is really back at the branch.',
    'parcel_received_back_s2' => 'Open the order. You will see that the courier returned the parcel.',
    'parcel_received_back_s3' => 'If you want, write something in the “Note (staff only)” box.',
    'parcel_received_back_s4' => 'Press “Parcel received back”.',
    'parcel_received_back_o1' => 'The goods go back into stock. The order closes when nothing else is left on it.',
    'parcel_received_back_o2' => 'No commission is paid for a returned parcel.',
    'parcel_received_back_o3' => 'The dealer gets a notice to contact the office about the order.',
    'parcel_received_back_t1' => 'Only staff with the stock permission can see this button.',
    'parcel_received_back_w1' => 'If the dealer paid, choose “Money only” in “Cancel, return and refund” on the order to give the money back. If you do not, the dealer does not get the money back.',
    'mixed_delivery_decision_s1' => 'Open the order. Under “Commission on the delivered goods”, see the value of what arrived and the order total.',
    'mixed_delivery_decision_s2' => 'If it says commission was added, there is nothing more to do.',
    'mixed_delivery_decision_s3' => 'An order whose commission was not added by itself waits on the “Decision needed” tab of “Deliveries”. Open that tab.',
    'mixed_delivery_decision_s4' => 'In the “Commission” box choose “Commission on the delivered part only” or “No commission, money goes to the company profit fund”. Write the reason and press “Save decision”.',
    'mixed_delivery_decision_s5' => 'To give no commission on an order at all, open the order and press “Give no commission”. Write the reason.',
    'mixed_delivery_decision_o1' => 'Partners see the value of what arrived and the reason on the order page.',
    'mixed_delivery_decision_t1' => 'Only staff with the order review permission can make this decision.',
    'mixed_delivery_decision_w1' => 'You cannot change the decision after you save it. If you give no commission, all of it goes to the company profit fund. Commission that partners already got is taken back.',
    'manual_couriers_s1' => 'Owner: switch these couriers on in “Settings” → “SMS and courier connections”. A dealer can then pick one when ordering.',
    'manual_couriers_s2' => 'After approval you get a notice saying to send by hand. Give the parcel to the courier.',
    'manual_couriers_s3' => 'Open the order. In the courier part, choose the “New step”.',
    'manual_couriers_s4' => 'Type the “Consignment number” and press “Save update”.',
    'manual_couriers_s5' => 'Change the step each time you hear from the courier. A step can only move forward, never back.',
    'manual_couriers_s6' => 'When the goods have really arrived, press “Confirm delivery”.',
    'manual_couriers_o1' => 'The dealer sees the step and the consignment number on the order page.',
    'manual_couriers_t1' => 'Sundarban and Janani have their own tracking page. The dealer can open it from the order.',
    'manual_couriers_w1' => 'The system cannot hear from these couriers by itself. If you do not change the step, the dealer keeps seeing the old one.',
    'inventory_branches_s1' => 'Open “Stock” in the “Products & stock” menu. You can see how much of each product you have.',
    'inventory_branches_s2' => 'When goods arrive, press “Product in”. Write how much came, and choose a reason.',
    'inventory_branches_s3' => 'When goods leave or get spoiled, press “Product out”. Choose a reason, such as “Damaged”. To fix a mistake in the count, choose the reason “Correction”.',
    'inventory_branches_s4' => 'To stop orders for a product for a while, press “Pause ordering” beside it. To start again, press “Resume ordering”.',
    'inventory_branches_s5' => 'To send goods from one branch to another, press “Move to another branch” beside the product. The rest happens in the “Branch transfers” tab of the “Batches & expiry” page.',
    'inventory_branches_s6' => 'To open a new branch, go to “Branches” and press “Add branch”. Write the code, name and address.',
    'inventory_branches_s7' => 'To give a branch its staff, press “Add staff”. Choose the job: manager, storekeeper or goods sender.',
    'inventory_branches_s8' => 'When you send an order, choose the branch the goods will go from.',
    'inventory_branches_o1' => 'The product list shows what is really in the store.',
    'inventory_branches_o2' => 'Every active branch has a staff member in charge.',
    'inventory_branches_o3' => 'Every sent order shows which branch the goods went from.',
    'inventory_branches_o4' => 'Goods that have left for delivery show as “With courier”. They are not counted in stock. If they come back, they are added to stock again.',
    'inventory_branches_t1' => 'Pause ordering before you change the stock of many products at once.',
    'inventory_branches_t2' => 'Do not change a branch code. Reports show this code.',
    'inventory_branches_t3' => 'Write down the opening stock when a new branch starts.',
    'inventory_branches_t4' => 'To get the list of all products as a PDF, press “Print stock”. The product photos are now bigger than before.',
    'inventory_branches_w1' => 'You cannot delete a branch that has stock or old orders. If needed, turn the branch off instead.',
    'inventory_branches_w2' => 'Do not change the stock of one product from two places at the same time. The records will get mixed up.',
    'inventory_branches_w3' => 'You cannot enter more than 10,00,000 units at one time. The system stops a wrong number.',
    'branch_performance_s1' => 'Open “Branch sales” in the “Reports” menu.',
    'branch_performance_s2' => 'Choose the time: “Today”, “This month” or “Choose dates”.',
    'branch_performance_s3' => 'If you chose your own dates, press “Show”.',
    'branch_performance_s4' => 'Pick one branch, or leave “All branches”.',
    'branch_performance_s5' => 'Read the totals at the top: orders, delivered order value, money collected, awaiting payment, and estimated profit.',
    'branch_performance_s6' => 'See each order in the list below. To search, type an order number, a name or a code.',
    'branch_performance_s7' => 'To get every order in an Excel file, press “Download (Excel)”. You see this button only if you have the reports permission.',
    'branch_performance_o1' => 'You can compare the branches for the same period.',
    'branch_performance_o2' => 'An order with no branch chosen shows separately as “Not set”.',
    'branch_performance_o3' => 'If a product has no purchase cost written, its profit may show as zero. This way the mistake is easy to see.',
    'branch_performance_t1' => 'Profit = (selling price − purchase cost) × quantity. So keep the “Purchase cost” of every product right.',
    'branch_performance_t2' => 'Each day is counted by company time. Keep this in mind when you choose dates.',
    'branch_performance_t3' => 'Branch staff see only the figures of their own branch.',
    'branch_performance_w1' => 'Do not treat the estimated profit as a final figure. It is not an audited profit and loss statement.',
    'branch_performance_w2' => 'Order value, money and profit count only goods that were delivered. Goods that were sent but have not arrived yet are left out.',
    'product_facts_s1' => 'Open “Products” in the “Products & stock” menu. Choose the product and edit it.',
    'product_facts_s2' => 'Fill every box that has a star. Boxes marked “optional” can be left empty.',
    'product_facts_s3' => 'In “Product facts for the website”, write: manufacturer, registration number, efficacy, ingredients, how to use (dose), warnings and how to store it.',
    'product_facts_s4' => 'The Bangla and English boxes sit side by side. When you write in English, the Bangla box may fill itself. Read the Bangla and correct it.',
    'product_facts_s5' => 'In “Health concern tags”, tick the tags that fit the product. If you need a new tag, press “Add tag”.',
    'product_facts_s6' => 'Under the product name, write the size in the “Pack size” box, for example “100 ml”. You can change it any time.',
    'product_facts_s7' => 'If the product comes in other sizes, press “Change size” in the “Other sizes of this product” part.',
    'product_facts_s8' => 'At the end, press “Save product”.',
    'product_facts_o1' => 'The product page on the website shows only the facts you wrote.',
    'product_facts_o2' => 'A box you leave empty does not show on the website, and neither does its heading.',
    'product_facts_t1' => 'Copy the registration number exactly from the certificate. If there is no certificate, leave the box empty.',
    'product_facts_t2' => 'The product saves even if you leave out manufacturer, group, efficacy, how to use and expiry date.',
    'product_facts_w1' => 'In a tag, write only the topic, for example “Digestion”. Never write that a product cures or treats an illness. The system refuses a tag like that.',
    'product_facts_w2' => 'Write only what is true and what you can prove.',
    'product_reviews_s1' => 'You get a notice when a new review arrives.',
    'product_reviews_s2' => 'Open “Customer reviews” in the “Website” menu.',
    'product_reviews_s3' => 'Read each review that is “Pending”.',
    'product_reviews_s4' => 'Press “Update status”. Choose “Approved” or “Rejected”, then save.',
    'product_reviews_o1' => 'Only the reviews you approve show on the website.',
    'product_reviews_t1' => 'Look at the pending reviews once a day so they do not pile up.',
    'product_reviews_w1' => 'Reject any review that says the product cured an illness or treated a disease.',
    'stock_batches_s1' => 'Write the batch number when you add stock or receive goods from a purchase.',
    'stock_batches_s2' => 'Write the expiry date if you know it. It is fine to leave it out.',
    'stock_batches_s3' => 'Open “Batches & expiry” in the “Products & stock” menu.',
    'stock_batches_s4' => 'In the “Expiring soon” tab, choose 30, 60 or 90 days. You will see which goods expire in that time.',
    'stock_batches_s5' => 'To choose how early you want a warning, pick from “Warn me this many days before expiry” and press “Save”.',
    'stock_batches_s6' => 'Expired goods show in a separate list. They can no longer be sent.',
    'stock_batches_s7' => 'To remove expired goods, press “Product out”. Choose the reason “Expired stock”.',
    'stock_batches_s8' => 'In the “Missing details” tab, see which batches have no number. Read the number on the pack, write it, and press “Fill in”.',
    'stock_batches_o1' => 'Stock staff get a notice when a batch is close to expiry or has expired.',
    'stock_batches_o2' => 'Goods can come in without a batch number. They wait in the “Missing details” tab, and you can write it later.',
    'stock_batches_t1' => 'Buyers can check the batch number of a pack on the website page “Check a batch number”.',
    'stock_batches_w1' => 'If a branch has only expired goods, they cannot be sent.',
    'stock_batches_w2' => 'If you give no expiry date, you will get no expiry warning for those goods.',
    'purchasing_goods_s1' => 'In the “Suppliers” tab, press “Add supplier”. Write the name and contact.',
    'purchasing_goods_s2' => 'In the “Purchase orders” tab, press “New purchase order”. Choose the supplier, the branch the goods will come to, the products and the quantity. Then press “Save as draft”.',
    'purchasing_goods_s3' => 'When the order has been given to the supplier, press “Mark as sent to supplier”.',
    'purchasing_goods_s4' => 'When goods arrive, open the order and go to “Receive goods”. Write only what came today: the quantity and the “Cost per unit”.',
    'purchasing_goods_s5' => 'Write the batch number and expiry date if you know them. It is fine to leave them out. Then press “Add to stock”.',
    'purchasing_goods_s6' => 'If the rest comes later, receive it the same way. The order shows “Ordered”, “Received” and “Still due”.',
    'purchasing_goods_s7' => 'To close an order, press “Cancel order”. Write the reason.',
    'purchasing_goods_s8' => 'If you no longer buy from a supplier, press “Archive supplier” beside them. Their name stays on old orders.',
    'purchasing_goods_o1' => 'Goods that arrive go into the stock of the branch they were meant for. Batch and expiry are kept if you wrote them.',
    'purchasing_goods_o2' => 'The order page has a list of what has arrived so far. You can also see who received it and when.',
    'purchasing_goods_t1' => 'Only staff who are allowed to see purchase costs can see the cost per unit.',
    'purchasing_goods_w1' => 'You cannot receive more goods than what is still due on the order.',
    'purchasing_goods_w2' => 'If you cancel an order, goods that already arrived stay in stock.',
    'stock_counting_s1' => 'Choose the branch and press “Start a count”.',
    'stock_counting_s2' => 'Write what you counted next to each product. Leave empty any product you did not count. Its stock will not change.',
    'stock_counting_s3' => 'Press “Save counts”. Then press “Send for approval”.',
    'stock_counting_s4' => 'Another staff member with approval permission approves it. It does not wait for the owner. They open the count and look at it.',
    'stock_counting_s5' => 'Before approving, a page opens. See how many products will go up or down.',
    'stock_counting_s6' => 'A yellow mark on a line means the stock of that product changed after the count. Check those lines, then tick “I have checked the lines that changed”.',
    'stock_counting_s7' => 'Press “Approve and update stock”. Then press “Yes, change the stock”. If you do not agree, press “Reject”. The stock will not change.',
    'stock_counting_s8' => 'If you started a count by mistake, press “Cancel this count”.',
    'stock_counting_o1' => 'Goods sold or received between the count and the approval are not touched. Only the gap between the count and the figure at that time is posted.',
    'stock_counting_o2' => 'When it is approved, the stock is corrected. When it is rejected, the stock stays as it was.',
    'stock_counting_t1' => 'If a branch has no approved count for 30 days, it shows “Overdue for a count”. Stock staff get a notice.',
    'stock_counting_t2' => 'Count the fast-selling products every week.',
    'stock_counting_w1' => 'A branch can have only one count open at a time. Finish or cancel the old one first.',
    'stock_counting_w2' => 'The person who took part in a count cannot approve it. Another staff member approves it. Only the owner may approve a count they took part in.',
    'batches_on_hold_s1' => 'Open “Batches & expiry” in the “Products & stock” menu. Then go to the “On hold” tab.',
    'batches_on_hold_s2' => 'Write the batch number, product name or product code, and press “Search”.',
    'batches_on_hold_s3' => 'Press “Put on hold” beside the batch. Write the reason.',
    'batches_on_hold_s4' => 'When the problem is solved, press “Release”. The goods can be sent again.',
    'batches_on_hold_s5' => 'If the goods cannot be used any more, press “Write off”.',
    'batches_on_hold_o1' => 'The batch shows “On hold”. You can also see who held it, since when, and why.',
    'batches_on_hold_t1' => 'If you doubt a batch, hold it right away. You can release it later.',
    'batches_on_hold_w1' => 'If you write off a batch, all its goods leave the stock. This cannot be undone.',
    'website_customization_s1' => 'To change banners, pictures or text, open “Arrange the website” in the “Website” menu. You need permission for this.',
    'website_customization_s2' => 'Show only products that are in stock on the home page. Edit the product and choose “Yes” or “No” in “Show on home page?”.',
    'website_customization_s3' => 'Write the main page text and notices on the “Page text” page.',
    'website_customization_s4' => 'See the enquiries from the website on the “Website enquiries” page in the “Messages & support” menu.',
    'website_customization_s5' => 'After you reply, press “Update status”. Choose the new status.',
    'website_customization_s6' => 'See applications from people who want to become partners on the “Dealer applications” and “Sub-dealer applications” pages in the “New partner applications” menu.',
    'website_customization_s7' => 'After you save a change, open the website on a phone and a computer to check it.',
    'website_customization_o1' => 'The website shows current offers and products that are in stock.',
    'website_customization_o2' => 'Enquiries gather in one list. You can answer them one by one.',
    'website_customization_o3' => 'A tidy website gives new dealers the confidence to join.',
    'website_customization_t1' => 'Always use the real company logo and photos.',
    'website_customization_t2' => 'The phone number, address and map are in the “Footer and contact” part. Keep them right.',
    'website_customization_t3' => 'When you upload pictures or videos, follow the limits on file size and type.',
    'website_customization_w1' => 'Do not show links meant only for staff in the public menu.',
    'website_customization_w2' => 'Never put a message asking for money on the website.',
    'website_editor_s1' => 'Open “Arrange the website” in the “Website” menu.',
    'website_editor_s2' => 'Choose a part: “Home page”, “Other pages”, “Text and policies”, “Videos” or “Footer and contact”.',
    'website_editor_s3' => 'To find a box, type its name in the search box at the top, for example “phone number”.',
    'website_editor_s4' => 'Write in the English box. A Bangla box sits with it. It may fill itself. Read the Bangla and correct it.',
    'website_editor_s5' => 'When you finish, press “Save site setup” in the bar at the bottom. The bar says “Changes not saved yet” or “Everything is saved”.',
    'website_editor_s6' => 'All video work is in the “Videos” part. The home page video has its own Save button. The big Save below does not save it.',
    'website_editor_s7' => 'To choose which products show first on the home page, use the list “Order of products on the home page” in the “Home page” part. Type a number or press the arrows. Then press “Save the order”.',
    'website_editor_o1' => 'When you save, your change goes to the website.',
    'website_editor_o2' => 'If the Bangla box is filled, Bangla readers see that. If it is empty, they see the earlier text.',
    'website_editor_t1' => 'After you save, check the page on a phone and a computer.',
    'website_editor_t2' => 'You can also put a number in the “Place on the home page” box when you edit a product.',
    'website_editor_w1' => 'If you press “Reset all to default text”, all your text is erased and the starting text comes back. This cannot be undone.',
    'website_editor_w2' => 'If the home page shows a “separate list”, this order is not used. Then choose the first option under “Which products to show” and save.',
    'trust_pages_s1' => 'In the “Pages” tab, change the title and text of each page. If you leave a box empty, the draft text is used.',
    'trust_pages_s2' => 'To show a page, tick “Show this page on the website”.',
    'trust_pages_s3' => 'In the “Business details” tab, write every number exactly as on the paper. Only the boxes you fill will show.',
    'trust_pages_s4' => 'In the “Complaint contact” tab, write a name. Then the contact part shows on the complaint page.',
    'trust_pages_s5' => 'In the “Partner registration form” tab, write the job titles for the three signatures on the form.',
    'trust_pages_s6' => 'In the “Quality documents” tab, upload a PDF or a picture. It must not be bigger than 10 MB.',
    'trust_pages_s7' => 'In the “Health articles” tab, press “New article” and write. Then press “Publish on the website”.',
    'trust_pages_o1' => 'Visitors see only what you have filled in and switched on.',
    'trust_pages_o2' => 'When a complaint comes from the website, it gets a “tracking number”, and you get a notice.',
    'trust_pages_t1' => 'Read every draft text before you rely on it.',
    'trust_pages_t2' => 'You and your lawyer write the page on leaving the partnership. It has no draft. It stays hidden until you write the text.',
    'trust_pages_t3' => 'The “Quality documents” page stays hidden until at least one document is shown. The articles page stays hidden until at least one article is published.',
    'trust_pages_w1' => 'Never write that a product or a treatment cures an illness.',
    'trust_pages_w2' => 'Do not write a number or licence detail that you have not checked against the paper.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_s1' => 'Open “Sales kit” in the “For partners” menu.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_s2' => 'Give a title, the type (poster, price list or social post), the language and the file. The file can be a PDF or a picture, up to 10 MB. Then press “Add file”.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_s3' => 'To change a file or its details, press “Edit”. Write the reason. To take a file away, press “Remove”.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_s4' => 'Open “Schemes” in the “For partners” menu. Write the scheme name, start and end dates, products, minimum quantity, benefit type, and what the partner gets.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_s5' => 'Press “Save scheme”. Partners see running schemes when they order.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_s6' => 'To change a scheme, press “Edit”. Write the reason. If its free goods have already gone out on an order, you can change only the name, the text and the end date.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_o1' => 'Partners see only approved files and schemes that are running now.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_o2' => 'A partner\'s menu shows “Sales kit” only when it has at least one file.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_t1' => 'What the partner gets is shown exactly as you write it.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_w1' => 'A scheme does not change the price, the order total or the commission.',
    'sales_kit_schemes_owner_w2' => 'If you choose “Free goods”, the free item is added once, at no price, to an order that meets the condition. No commission is paid on it. If no free goods are given, the office must give the benefit by hand.',
    'finance_treasury_s1' => 'Open “Treasury” from the menu. On the “Funds” tab you will see one card for each fund.',
    'finance_treasury_s2' => 'Tap a card. You will see what came in, what went out, and what is in it now.',
    'finance_treasury_s3' => 'Look at the “Company profit” card. Money that nobody received lands here, for example when there is no referrer or no area dealer. Every line says why.',
    'finance_treasury_s4' => 'To spend money, open the fund and press “Spend”. If staff write the spend, another staff member approves it on the “Spending, budgets & pending work” tab. A spend at or above the owner\'s limit waits for the owner. The owner can approve it alone.',
    'finance_treasury_s5' => 'The “Event log” box on the “Other modules” page lists orders, money received, commission, withdrawals and stock. Use the filter to pick one kind.',
    'finance_treasury_s6' => 'On the “Partners\' money” tab, see each dealer and sub-dealer with their money now and total earned. Anything waiting for someone is on the “Spending, budgets & pending work” tab.',
    'finance_treasury_s7' => 'Only the owner sees the “Profit and loss” tab. Pick a month or dates to see the profit or loss after the cost of goods, commission and salaries.',
    'finance_treasury_o1' => 'You can tap any figure to see the lines behind it.',
    'finance_treasury_o2' => 'You know where every taka of the company is right now.',
    'finance_treasury_t1' => 'Cards always show the total up to today. Changing the dates only changes the list below.',
    'finance_treasury_t2' => 'Commission is shared only after an order is delivered. So do not look for the money in funds before delivery.',
    'finance_treasury_w1' => 'Do not post pictures of this page in a partners\' group.',
    'finance_treasury_w2' => 'If product buying costs are missing, the profit figure will be wrong. The page warns you about products with no cost.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_s1' => 'Open “Commission rules & rates” from the menu.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_s2' => 'On the “Set commission shares” tab, see all the rates now in use.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_s3' => 'To change a rate, get written approval first. Also fix a start date.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_s4' => 'Open the “Commission calculator” tab.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_s5' => 'Type in a sample order. See who gets how much. Try both the dealer price and the sub-dealer price.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_s6' => 'Tell the dealers in advance with a notice. After the new rate starts, watch the first few orders.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_o1' => 'The calculator shows who would get what, but no money moves.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_o2' => 'An impossible split is caught before the rate changes.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_t1' => 'Keep a notebook with every change and its date.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_t2' => 'When a rate changes, also check what changes for salary, royalty and rank prizes.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_w1' => 'Never pay anyone because of what the calculator shows.',
    'finance_policies_simulator_w2' => 'Do not change old saved splits to match the new rule.',
    'payouts_settlements_s1' => 'Open “Withdrawal requests” from the menu. The “Still to do” filter shows late and held requests.',
    'payouts_settlements_s2' => 'Press “Review” next to a request. Check the partner\'s status, balance, number and NID.',
    'payouts_settlements_s3' => 'If all is well, press “Approve request”. If not, press “Reject request” and write the reason.',
    'payouts_settlements_s4' => 'Choose who will send the money. If it is you, press “I will pay”.',
    'payouts_settlements_s5' => 'Send the money to the number the partner asked for. Then press “Record payment” and add the transaction number and a picture of the receipt.',
    'payouts_settlements_s6' => 'If you have no receipt yet, choose “Money sent, receipt later”. Press “Add receipt” when you have it.',
    'payouts_settlements_s7' => 'At month end, open “Month end: pay commission & salary” from the menu. Salary and royalty for a month usually close on their own within an hour. For an older month, press “Close this month”.',
    'payouts_settlements_o1' => 'Each payment shows who paid, when, and the receipt.',
    'payouts_settlements_o2' => 'For a closed month, you can see how much went to partners.',
    'payouts_settlements_t1' => 'A partner can cancel a request that is still waiting. The money then goes back to the wallet. The owner can prepare, approve and pay alone.',
    'payouts_settlements_t2' => 'After a phone number or password change, the partner usually cannot withdraw for 2 hours. This is for safety.',
    'payouts_settlements_w1' => 'Never send money without matching the account number.',
    'payouts_settlements_w2' => 'If a partner\'s account is suspended, the request is held. It cannot be approved or paid until the account is active again.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_s1' => 'Open “Other modules” from the menu and press the “Event log” box. It shows who approved what, and when.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_s2' => 'Search by name, order number or date.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_s3' => 'Use the “Type” filter to pick one kind, for example only withdrawals.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_s4' => 'To see who changed what, open “Work log” under “Settings”.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_o1' => 'You can follow one order from the day it was placed to delivery and commission.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_o2' => 'You can find out who made a change and when.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_t1' => 'Search by order number to see everything about that order together.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_w1' => 'What is written here cannot be changed or deleted.',
    'financial_activation_gates_s1' => 'While live is off, the calculator and many partner pages still work. But no real dues or income are saved.',
    'financial_activation_gates_s2' => 'Before going live, open “Check opening balances” in Settings. See there whether everything is ready.',
    'financial_activation_gates_s3' => 'If there are no old balances, open the “Start the books” card on the owner home page. Tick the box and press “Start the books from zero”.',
    'financial_activation_gates_s4' => 'The owner can check the starting balances and commission rules alone. If staff prepared them, the owner or another approver checks.',
    'financial_activation_gates_s5' => 'Turn live on only in the agreed way. Never change it on the server in a hurry.',
    'financial_activation_gates_s6' => 'Tell the dealers by notice, with the exact date and time. Watch the books and payments closely on day one.',
    'financial_activation_gates_o1' => 'Everyone knows whether the money books are live or in trial.',
    'financial_activation_gates_o2' => 'Before going live there is written approval and proof of readiness.',
    'financial_activation_gates_o3' => 'Support staff can explain why money is switched off. They do not make up a start date.',
    'financial_activation_gates_t1' => 'Always keep live money off on a demo system.',
    'financial_activation_gates_t2' => 'When going live, check that backups work. Also plan how to stop if needed.',
    'financial_activation_gates_w1' => 'Do not go live just to fix empty balances when the information is incomplete.',
    'financial_activation_gates_w2' => 'Never run demo data on the real business system.',
    'financial_activation_gates_w3' => 'The switch that pays commission automatically after its waiting days is separate. Only the owner can change it.',
    'accounting_statements_s1' => 'Open “Treasury”, then the “Order report” tab. Pick the dates you need.',
    'accounting_statements_s2' => 'Press “Download”.',
    'accounting_statements_s3' => 'Choose “Profit and loss”, “Balance sheet” or “Trial balance”.',
    'accounting_statements_o1' => 'The file holds the figures for exactly the dates you picked.',
    'accounting_statements_t1' => 'Give the files to your accountant every month.',
    'accounting_statements_w1' => 'These files are not yet the full books. Some sales and buying lines come from other records, and some are estimates. Do not call them audited accounts.',
    'accounting_statements_w2' => 'The files hold company figures. Keep them private.',
    'menu_office_s1' => 'Top rows: “Dashboard”, “Orders”, “Check order payments”, “Deliveries”, “Messages & support”.',
    'menu_office_s2' => 'Money rows: “Treasury”, “Withdrawal requests”, “Month end: pay commission & salary”.',
    'menu_office_s3' => 'Work rows: “Products and stock”, “Dealers and sub-dealers”, “New partner applications”, “Reports”, “Prescriptions”.',
    'menu_office_s4' => 'Commission rules & rates, the event log, schemes, training, staff, the website and the user guide are now on the “Other modules” page.',
    'menu_office_s5' => '“Settings” is at the bottom. Money, area and system rules are there.',
    'menu_office_s6' => 'When a row holds several pages, small tabs appear at the top of the page. Tap a tab to change page.',
    'menu_office_o1' => 'Only the pages you are allowed to open show in the menu.',
    'menu_office_t1' => 'Type a page name in “Search menu” to go straight to it.',
    'menu_office_w1' => 'If a page is missing from your menu, it is not broken. You do not have permission for it. Ask the owner.',
    'settings_home_s1' => 'Open “Settings”. You will see three groups: “Money”, “Areas and partners” and “System”.',
    'settings_home_s2' => 'Money: withdrawal rules, bKash and bank numbers, and checking the opening money figures.',
    'settings_home_s3' => 'Area and partners: area codes, what shows on partner dashboards, and whether one person has two accounts.',
    'settings_home_s4' => 'System: login rules, when a reason must be written, SMS and courier connections, courier areas.',
    'settings_home_s5' => 'System also has: bringing data from Excel, the work log, data requests, clearing old data and the site problem list.',
    'settings_home_s6' => 'Open a box, change the boxes you need, then tap “Save”.',
    'settings_home_o1' => 'Read the box text first and you will know what the page does.',
    'settings_home_t1' => 'A box you cannot see is outside your work. It is not broken.',
    'settings_home_w1' => 'Be sure before you save. A change here reaches everyone at once.',
    'office_more_pages_s1' => 'Open “Other modules”. Tap a box to open that page.',
    'office_more_pages_s2' => 'For partners: “Schemes”, “Contests”, “Sales kit”, “Training”, “Meetings” and “Agreement”.',
    'office_more_pages_s3' => 'Staff and people: “Staff list”, “Staff salary”, “SR areas & targets”, “Field sales”, “Roles & permissions”.',
    'office_more_pages_s4' => 'In the staff list, add the new person’s name, phone, role and branch. After you save, the first password shows once. Write it down and give it to them.',
    'office_more_pages_s5' => 'Website: “Arrange the website”, “Page text”, “Trust pages”, “Videos”, “Feedback” and “Website visitors” (the same page also shows which dealers and sub-dealers are online now, with their last IP address, device and browser).',
    'office_more_pages_s6' => 'When you approve a review, it shows on the website.',
    'office_more_pages_s7' => 'Clinic: “Prescriptions”.',
    'office_more_pages_s8' => 'Look at new applications under “New partner applications” in the menu. Check the application number, age and any earlier account there.',
    'office_more_pages_s9' => 'Money and records: “Commission rules & rates” and “Event log”. The event log shows who approved what, and when.',
    'office_more_pages_s10' => 'Help: “User guide and tour”. Press it to open the guide.',
    'office_more_pages_o1' => 'All the pages you use less often are in one place.',
    'office_more_pages_t1' => 'Tap the help sign on any page to see that page’s rules first.',
    'office_more_pages_w1' => 'Approving an application creates a real account. Check the papers first.',
    'menu_partner_s1' => '“Home” is your dashboard. You see your photo, mobile, code, rank, total income, current balance, this month’s purchase, what is left to reach the target, and your area of responsibility. Use the “Sign out” button at the top (on a phone, open the menu and use “Sign out” at its top) to leave.',
    'menu_partner_s2' => 'Start an order from “New order”. Past orders and deliveries are in “My orders”.',
    'menu_partner_s3' => '“Wallet” is one page. It shows how much money you have, where it came from and what you took out.',
    'menu_partner_s4' => 'A sub-dealer’s salary lines are also in “Wallet”. Pick “Salary” in the list filter.',
    'menu_partner_s5' => '“My team & customers” has team, customers, rank, top sellers and contests. For sub-dealers the row is called “My customers” and has customers, top sellers and contests.',
    'menu_partner_s6' => '“Other modules” has training, meetings, sales kit and give feedback. The agreement is inside “My profile” or “My account”.',
    'menu_partner_s7' => '“Contact the office” has messages, notices and help.',
    'menu_partner_s8' => '“My profile” has all your details (view only) and security. Change your password here. “My account” lists every income of yours on its own line. “Prescriptions” always stays in the menu, for those who may use it.',
    'menu_partner_o1' => 'You find every page without searching.',
    'menu_partner_t1' => 'Type a page name in “Search menu” to go straight to it.',
    'menu_partner_w1' => 'If a page is not in your menu, it is switched off for your account. Ask the office.',
    'website_editor_s8' => 'To choose which product comes first on the home page, type a number or use the arrows in the “Order of products on the home page” list. Then press “Save the order”. The same list is also under “Products & stock” → “Products”.',
    'product_facts_s9' => 'The pack size (for example 100 ml) is in the “Pack size” box under the product name. You can change it at any time after the product is made.',
    'office_dashboard_badge' => 'Dashboard',
    'office_dashboard_title' => 'Dashboard: the buttons and the lists',
    'office_dashboard_summary' => 'At the top of the dashboard are two buttons. Under them are today’s numbers, and under those is one area of lists. Press a list name to open that list.',
    'office_dashboard_purpose' => 'Your daily work can start from one page, so you do not have to hunt for other pages.',
    'office_dashboard_why' => 'A list that is outside your work is not shown. If you see fewer lists than someone else, nothing is broken.',
    'office_dashboard_s1' => 'Press “Add a new dealer” at the top to open the new dealer form. Press “Add a new sub-dealer” to open the new sub-dealer form. Press “Add a new product” to open the new product form.',
    'office_dashboard_s2' => 'If a button is missing, you have not been given that permission. Ask the owner.',
    'office_dashboard_s3' => 'To find an order, type the order number, phone number or name in the order search box and press “Search”.',
    'office_dashboard_s4' => 'Under the number cards the list names are laid out: Orders, Accounts, Withdrawals, Payments to check, New applications, Low stock. Press the one you want to see.',
    'office_dashboard_s5' => 'To search a list, type a name, number or phone and press “Search”. If there are many rows, press “Next” and “Previous” under the list.',
    'office_dashboard_s6' => 'To see the whole list, press “See all” on the right of the list. Press the first word of a row to open that order or account.',
    'office_dashboard_s7' => 'Below are summary boxes: Money summary, Website analysis summary, Products and orders summary and Latest events. A box whose figures you may not see is not shown.',
    'office_dashboard_s8' => 'Press “See the full page” on the right of a box to open the whole page on that subject. The figures can take a few seconds to appear.',
    'office_dashboard_o1' => 'From the dashboard you can reach a new dealer, a new product or any order.',
    'office_dashboard_t1' => 'In the morning, look at “Payments to check” and “Withdrawals” first. Partners are waiting on these.',
    'office_dashboard_w1' => 'A list appears a moment after the page. Wait a second or two and do not press again and again.',
];
